1
00:00:00,511 --> 00:00:04,891
Every time you fill up, the station
makes about 13 cents a gallon.

2
00:00:04,911 --> 00:00:07,822
So why does it never stop selling you gas?

3
00:00:07,842 --> 00:00:12,022
Fill up fifteen gallons, and the
owner clears about two bucks.

4
00:00:12,042 --> 00:00:15,966
Your card swipe alone eats
8 cents of every gallon.

5
00:00:15,986 --> 00:00:18,286
Because gas isn't the business.

6
00:00:18,306 --> 00:00:20,143
Gas is the bait.

7
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:26,583
Fuel is 65% of what gas stations sell,
but only about 39% of their profit.

8
00:00:26,603 --> 00:00:31,883
The rest comes from inside: coffee,
hot dogs, energy drinks and snacks.

9
00:00:31,903 --> 00:00:35,793
And 57% of drivers who
fill up walk right in.

10
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:40,034
So that big price sign? Its real
job is getting you off the road.

11
00:00:40,054 --> 00:00:42,534
Your coffee pays for the gas.
